  timon project update <slug> [--name TEXT] [--cwd PATH] [--workspace NAME] [--create-workspace]
                       [--color #RRGGBB] [--icon TEXT] [--speech TEXT] [--kind TEXT] [--status TEXT]
                                             edits what you pass; an empty value clears workspace, speech, icon, kind
  timon workspace list [--json]                workspaces (poles) with their lead agent and projects
  timon project demo                           creates the demo project (a small sample repository)

Routines (cron → creates a Kanban task on each due tick):
  timon routine list
  timon routine create --name TEXT --agent NAME --cron EXPR --prompt TEXT [--type ...] [--project SLUG]
  timon routine update <id> [--cron ...] [--enabled true|false] ...
  timon routine delete <id>

Workflows (graphs of nodes — agents, conditions, waits — run from a published version):
  timon workflow list                          workflows you can see (json)
  timon workflow get <slug>                    one workflow, with its draft
  timon workflow create --file FILE            creates a workflow from a JSON definition
  timon workflow publish <slug>                publishes the draft as the next version
  timon workflow run <slug> [--input JSON]     starts a run of the published version
  timon workflow runs <slug>                   the runs of a workflow
  timon workflow status <run_id>               a run with its nodes, definition and spans
  timon workflow cancel <run_id>               stops a run
  timon workflow import pipeline|agent|routine <id>
                                             turns a pipeline, an agent or a routine into a workflow
  timon workflow node done --output JSON [--route PORT]
                                             closes the current node of a run from inside its mission
                                             (reads TIMON_WORKFLOW_RUN_ID and TIMON_WORKFLOW_NODE_ID)

Triggers (source → filter → actions, run unattended):
  timon trigger list [--source schedule|webhook|event]
  timon trigger create --source schedule --name TEXT --cron EXPR [--tz ZONE] --action JSON ...
  timon trigger create --source webhook --name TEXT --slug NAME --auth github|gitlab|standard|generic
                       [--filter JSON] --action JSON ...   prints the secret ONCE
  timon trigger create --source event --name TEXT --event KIND [--filter JSON] --action JSON ...
                       shortcuts instead of --action: --todo TEXT [--project SLUG] | --notify TITLE
                       | --task-agent NAME --prompt TEXT
                       | --script BIN [--arg A ...] --cwd DIR [--env SECRET ...] [--timeout SECONDS]
                         [--allow-overlap] [--no-failure-alert]   runs a program, no agent (scripts:run);
                         from an agent's mission it becomes a proposal the user approves
  timon trigger proposals [--status pending|applied|dismissed]
                                             scripts agents asked for, waiting for you
  timon trigger approve|reject <proposal-id> creates the trigger as yours, or drops it (never from a mission)
  timon trigger test <id|slug> [--payload JSON] [--header Name:Value ...] [--execute]
                                             dry run unless --execute
  timon trigger remove <id|slug>

Pipelines (multi-agent workflow templates → Kanban tasks):
  timon pipeline list
  timon pipeline get <id>
  timon pipeline create --name TEXT --file pipeline.json [--description D]
  timon pipeline run <id> [--input JSON | --input-file PATH]
  timon pipeline run-status <run_id>
  timon pipeline delete <id>

Agent messages (async inbox — doesn't block the parent's tokens):
  timon msg send <to_agent> <payload...>     fire-and-forget to an agent's inbox
                                            [--kind msg|request|response]
                                            [--in-reply-to <msg_id>]
                                            [--to-mission <mid>]
  timon msg recv [--to <agent>] [--from <agent>] [--status pending|picked] [--limit N]
  timon msg pick <message_id>                marks picked + returns the payload (atomic)
  timon msg reply <message_id> <payload...>  sends a response to the message's from_agent

Notifications (human center — sidebar canvas):
  timon notify report  <title…> [--body TEXT] [--task-id ID]    end-of-task report, result
  timon notify alert   <title…> [--body TEXT] [--urgent] [--task-id ID]   blocking alert
  timon notify action_required <title…> [--body TEXT] [--urgent] [--dismiss-on reply,task_done] [--ttl MIN]
                       closes by itself on the human's reply in the mission (default), the task's DONE, or after --ttl (default 24 h with no trigger, 7 days with one)
    --mission-id is auto-injected from TIMON_MISSION_ID if not provided.

PROJECT TO DO (a project's idea notebook — nothing here is ever dispatched):
  timon project-todo list [--status open|done|promoted|all] [--project SLUG] [--json]
  timon project-todo add <text...> [--project SLUG] [--notes TEXT]
  timon project-todo update <id> [<text...>] [--project SLUG] [--notes TEXT] [--status open|done]
  timon project-todo done <id> [--undo]        checks / unchecks the idea
  timon project-todo promote <id> --agent NAME [--type TYPE] [--priority N] [--base REF] [--pipeline P]
                                               the idea becomes a PENDING task, and keeps the link to it
  timon project-todo rm <id>

Users (daemon-token — the operator's account recovery; administering accounts is the Multi-user
plugin's, from its page in the app):
  timon setup-token                          one-time token the first-run form asks for on an exposed install
  timon user list                            accounts (json)
  timon user reset-password <email-or-id>    temporary password, printed once

Paired devices (another Timon that drives this machine — a headless server has no screen to click):
  timon device pair [--user EMAIL-OR-ID] [--json]
                                             one-time pairing code (5 min) + this daemon's tailnet
                                             address; --user: a superadmin issues it for that account
  timon device list [--json]                 devices, their state and last connection
  timon device rename <id> <name>
  timon device revoke <id>                   cut off at once; pair again with a new code

Subscription accounts (superadmin / daemon-token — who may use which account):
  timon backend-account list [--json]        accounts, their state and who they are assigned to
  timon backend-account grant <id> --user EMAIL-OR-ID[,…]
                                             lets these users use the account (adds to the list)
  timon backend-account revoke <id> --user EMAIL-OR-ID[,…]
                                             takes it back from them
      <id> is the account id or its instance (claude@<id>); signing in stays in the app.

Backends you add yourself (a person's gesture: a mission's token is refused with operator_only):
  timon backend add <name> --base-url URL --protocol anthropic|openai-responses
                    [--key-from-stdin | --no-key] [--id ID] [--models A,B]
                    [--default-model SLUG] [--brand KEY] [--icon VALUE] [--json]
      the key is NEVER an argument: a terminal asks for it (input hidden), or pipe it:
        printf %s "$KEY" | timon backend add DeepSeek --base-url https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic \\
          --protocol anthropic --key-from-stdin
      it goes to the vault, reserved to this backend, and is never shown again.
  timon backend list [--json]                the backends you added, their state, never a key
  timon backend test <id> [--json]           one call to its model listing, with its saved key;
                                             exit code 0 only if the endpoint accepts the key
  timon backend test --base-url URL --protocol anthropic|openai-responses
                    [--key-from-stdin | --no-key] [--json]
                                             the same, before saving anything
  timon backend rm <id> [--json]             removes it; a key added with it leaves the vault

Secrets vault (write-only: no command ever prints a stored value):
  timon secret list [--project SLUG] [--agent NAME] [--json]
  timon secret set <NAME> [--scope global|project:<slug>|agent:<name>]
                          [--mode inject|broker] [--note TEXT] --stdin
      the value is ALWAYS piped on stdin, never an argument:
        printf %s "$TOKEN" | timon secret set GITHUB_TOKEN --scope global --stdin
      no --scope at all = the daemon alone, which no agent ever receives.
  timon secret grant <NAME> --scope …        opens it to one more scope
      backend:<id> is a reservation, not an audience: the entry then reaches
      only that backend's own process, for the missions its other grants admit.
  timon secret revoke <NAME> --scope …       closes that scope again
  timon secret rm <NAME>
  timon secret rekey                         new master key, staged then promoted
  timon secret import-env [--delete-source]  imports ~/.timon/secrets.env, no grant

Backend sign-in (write-only: the stored token is never printed):
  timon auth claude-token set      reads the token printed by 'claude setup-token'
                                   from stdin, or asks for it (hidden) in a terminal:
        claude setup-token          # then paste the token when asked
        printf %s "$TOKEN" | timon auth claude-token set
      every claude mission receives it; needed on macOS for Timon to run with
      no session open. Then run 'timon service install' to switch the service.
  timon auth claude-token status   configured or not, never the value
  timon auth claude-token clear

Memory (rules injected into agents — DIRECT write to the database):
  timon memory rule add <text…> [--scope agent|project|role|global] [--agent NAME]
                               [--project SLUG] [--role ROLE]
                               [--kind pitfall|decision|preference] [--tier normal|core]
                               [--text-file PATH] [--json]
      defaults: --scope agent, --kind pitfall, agent = $TIMON_AGENT, project = $TIMON_PROJECT.
      This is THE way to memorize: writing to pieges.md no longer injects anything.
      An exact duplicate on the same scope is refused (exit 3).
  timon memory rule list [--scope …] [--agent NAME] [--project SLUG] [--json]
  timon memory rule rm <id>
  timon memory search <query…>                 cross-cutting search (rules + facts)
  timon memory overview                        counters + pending proposals
  timon memory show <project|agent> <id> [file]  reads the reference .md files

Project's embedded browser (NEVER a local Chrome — see system prompt):
  timon browser status [<slug>] [--json]     does the project have a browser up?
  timon browser start  [<slug>]              starts it (persistent profile, sessions kept)
  timon browser stop   [<slug>]              stops it (the profile itself survives)
  timon browser list   [--json]              all known sessions
  timon browser recording get <id>           the recording your conversion mission learns (that mission only)
  timon browser annotations get [<id>] [--batch <bab-…>] [--status pending|resolved|dismissed] [--json]
                                             annotations the user sent this mission (or its agent)
  timon browser annotations resolve <id> --summary "<what you changed>"
  timon browser annotations dismiss <id> --reason "<why not>"
    default slug: $TIMON_PROJECT, otherwise derived from cwd.

Widget arrangement of the user's screen (an agent's mission owner):
  timon widgets get [--view PATH] [--project SLUG]
                                             zones, cards, catalog, chat columns
  timon widgets propose [--view PATH] [--project SLUG] [--note TEXT] [--file F]
                                             a card the user applies (JSON on stdin)
  timon widgets preset-save <name> [--view PATH] [--project SLUG] [--replace]
                                             current arrangement → Layouts menu

Island workspace of the user's screen (an agent's mission owner):
  timon islands get [--view PATH] [--project SLUG]
                                             islands, tabs, focus, content types, limits
  timon islands propose [--view PATH] [--project SLUG] [--note TEXT] [--file F]
                                             a card the user applies (JSON on stdin:
                                             {open: {...}} or {layout: {...}})
  timon islands propose --arrangement ID [--view PATH] [--project SLUG] [--note TEXT]
                                             a card recalling a named arrangement on the view
  timon setup avatar|soul|team|finish        the main agent's own setup conversation (refused elsewhere)
  timon navigate routes                      pages of the app an agent can send the user to
  timon navigate go <path> [--param k=v]... [--note TEXT]
                                             ask the user to go there (a card they follow)
  timon ui-doc render <file.html> [--title TEXT] [--reply]
  timon ui-doc get <id>
                                             shows an HTML document as a card in this mission's chat
  timon nav get                              pages hidden from the side menu, and its layout
  timon nav propose [--hide <path>]... [--order <p,p,---,p>] [--footer <p,p>] [--note TEXT]
                                             proposes the complete list of hidden pages (no flag = show all),
                                             the main list and the bottom of the menu (--- = a separator)
  timon onboarding profile [set <developer|automation|beginner>]
                                             the onboarding profile of the account
  timon islands preset-save <name> [--view PATH] [--project SLUG] [--replace]
                                             current view (islands included) → Layouts menu
  timon islands arrangements [--full]        the account's named island arrangements
  timon islands arrangement-save <name> [--view PATH] [--project SLUG] [--file LAYOUT.json] [--replace]
                                             current islands of a view, or a layout ({root, focus?}),
                                             → Island arrangements menu (never the main menu)

Timon documentation (the pages of the installed version, read offline, no daemon needed):
  timon docs search <words…> [--limit N] [--json]
                                             pages that match, with an excerpt (same as docs_search)
  timon docs read [<route>] [--heading TEXT]  a page as Markdown, or one section of it; without a
                                             route, the list of every page (same as docs_read)

Resources (anti-saturation guard for the machine):
  timon export [--out F] [--with-archive]    portable archive of ~/.timon (secrets excluded)
  timon import F [--to DIR] [--force] [--no-projects]
                                             restores an archive on this machine
  timon backup enable                        nightly routine 03:30, on by default (re-arms it if turned off)
  timon backup status [--json]               state, next run, archives under backups/
  timon doctor [--json]                      binaries, host capabilities, config
  timon doctor --report [--save F]           diagnostic report to paste in a support request
  timon logs [--desktop|--prompts|--supervisor] [-n N]
                                             newest log lines first (default: daemon, 100)

Third-party plugins (hot-loaded, no daemon restart):
  timon plugin list [--json]                 installed, version, enabled, refused
  timon plugin add <spec> [--yes]            npm install (name, .tgz, .zip or dir)
  timon plugin remove <id>                   npm uninstall (data kept)
  timon plugin enable <id> | disable <id>    toggles in timon.config.json
  timon plugin check <dir> [--json] [--strict] [--deny <word>]…
                                             pre-ship check of a plugin folder: manifest, engines.node,
                                             signature, shipped files, author and machine data; never runs it
  timon plugin sign <dir>                    signs with ~/.timon-signing/plugins.key
  timon plugin verify <id>                   verifies without loading the plugin

Web app served by the daemon (NEVER an orchestrator restart):
  timon app status [--json]                  module active? app built? child alive?
  timon app restart                          signals the web-app child (or rearms a supervisor that gave up)

Daemon service (systemd user unit on Linux, launchd agent on macOS — a launchd
                daemon once a claude token is set —, scheduled task at boot on Windows):
  timon service install [--dry-run] [--allow-temp-home] [--force]
                                             writes the unit/plist and starts it; refuses a TIMON_HOME
                                             under the system temporary folder without the flag, and a
                                             service that belongs to another Timon installation without --force
  timon service uninstall [--force]          stops and removes it, ~/.timon untouched; same refusal
  timon service stop                         ends the daemon and its programs, keeps the service registered (Windows: the task is disabled); the app starts it again at its next launch
  timon service start                        starts a stopped service again
  timon service status [--json]              installed? running?
  timon service repair                       Windows: seals the session witness again when the service waits for a logon that never comes

Bundled modules (writes timon.config.json — effective on next daemon boot):
  timon module list [--json]                 catalog, wanted state, actual state + reason
  timon module enable <name> | disable <name>  toggles in timon.config.json

Secrets broker (the daemon acts, you never hold the value):
  git config credential.helper "timon git-credential"
                                             git then authenticates through the
                                             vault: no token in a remote URL,
                                             a command line or the environment

Offline license:
  timon license status                       status, edition and expiration
  timon license deactivate                   release this machine (the seat transfers once its last token lease expires)
  timon license install <file>               validates then installs the JWT
  timon license activate <key>               exchanges the key with the license server, then installs the JWT

  timon health [--json]                      day/night profile, Timon cgroups memory
                                            and CPU, live missions, OOM

Remote daemon:
  timon --daemon <url|name> <cmd> …       targets a daemon (URL or profile)
  timon daemon add <name> <url> <token>   profile in ~/.timon/cli-daemons.json (0600)
  timon daemon list                       profiles (url only, never the token)

Daemon address: --daemon > TIMON_API > timon.config.json daemon.listen
                > desktop-bootstrap.json daemonPort > http://localhost:3000
                Files are read under TIMON_HOME (default ~/.timon).
Authentication: named profile token, otherwise TIMON_API_TOKEN or daemon-token.
                daemon-token is only sent to the local listener, whether the
                target comes from --daemon <url> or TIMON_API.
                For remote URLs, set TIMON_API_TOKEN or use a named profile.
`,
  );
}

/* ─── shared helpers ─── */
async function readAll(stream) {
  const chunks = [];
  for await (const c of stream) chunks.push(c);
  return Buffer.concat(chunks).toString('utf8');
}

function takeFlag(argv, name) {
  // very small flag parser: --foo VALUE or --foo=VALUE
  for (let i = 0; i < argv.length; i++) {
    const a = argv[i];
    if (a === '--' + name) return argv.splice(i, 2)[1];
    if (a.startsWith('--' + name + '=')) return argv.splice(i, 1)[0].slice(name.length + 3);
  }
  return undefined;
}

async function readContent(argv, label) {
  const file = takeFlag(argv, 'file');
  if (file) {
    return fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8');
  }
  if (process.stdin.isTTY) {
    process.stderr.write(`timon: pipe the ${label} on stdin or pass --file PATH\n`);
    process.exit(64);
  }
  return await readAll(process.stdin);
}

/* ─── skills ─── */
async function cmdSkillList() {
  const j = await http('GET', '/api/skills');
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j.skills || [], null, 2) + '\n');
}
async function cmdSkillGet(argv) {
  const file = takeFlag(argv, 'file');
  const id = argv[0];
  if (!id) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon skill get <id> [--file PATH]\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  if (file) {
    const f = await http('GET', `/api/skills/${encodeURIComponent(id)}/file?path=${encodeURIComponent(file)}`);
    process.stdout.write((f.content || '') + '\n');
    return;
  }
  const j = await http('GET', `/api/skills/${encodeURIComponent(id)}`);
  process.stdout.write((j.content || '') + '\n');
  // On stderr: the body stays pipeable as it was.
  if (Array.isArray(j.files) && j.files.length > 0) {
    process.stderr.write(`files next to SKILL.md (timon skill get ${id} --file PATH): ${j.files.map((f) => f.path).join(', ')}\n`);
  }
}
async function cmdSkillPut(argv) {
  const id = argv.shift();
  if (!id) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon skill put <id> [--file PATH] [--create-only]  (or pipe content on stdin)\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const createOnly = argv.includes('--create-only');
  if (createOnly) argv.splice(argv.indexOf('--create-only'), 1);
  const content = await readContent(argv, 'SKILL.md body');
  if (!content.trim()) {
    process.stderr.write('timon: empty content\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const body = { id, content };
  if (createOnly) body.create_only = true;
  const j = await http('POST', '/api/skills', body);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j) + '\n');
}
async function cmdSkillRm(argv) {
  const id = argv[0];
  if (!id) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon skill rm <id>\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const j = await http('DELETE', `/api/skills/${encodeURIComponent(id)}`);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j) + '\n');
}

async function cmdSkillAttach(argv) {
  const exclude = argv.includes('--exclude');
  if (exclude) argv.splice(argv.indexOf('--exclude'), 1);
  const scope = takeFlag(argv, 'scope');
  const target = takeFlag(argv, 'target');
  const mode = takeFlag(argv, 'mode');
  const skill = argv[0];
  if (!skill || !scope) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon skill attach <id> --scope S [--target T] [--mode M] [--exclude]\n  S: global|project|role|agent   M: include|import\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const body = { skill, scope };
  if (target !== undefined) body.target = target;
  if (mode !== undefined) body.mode = mode;
  if (exclude) body.exclude = true;
  const j = await http('POST', '/api/skill-attachments', body);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j) + '\n');
}
async function cmdSkillDetach(argv) {
  const id = argv[0];
  if (!id) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon skill detach <attachment-id>\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const j = await http('DELETE', `/api/skill-attachments/${encodeURIComponent(id)}`);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j) + '\n');
}
async function cmdSkillAttachments(argv) {
  const q = new URLSearchParams();
  for (const key of ['scope', 'target', 'skill']) {
    const v = takeFlag(argv, key);
    if (v) q.set(key, v);
  }
  const qs = q.toString();
  const j = await http('GET', `/api/skill-attachments${qs ? `?${qs}` : ''}`);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j.attachments || [], null, 2) + '\n');
}
async function cmdSkillResolve(argv) {
  const agent = argv[0];
  if (!agent) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon skill resolve <agent>\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const j = await http('GET', `/api/agents/${encodeURIComponent(agent)}/skills`);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j, null, 2) + '\n');
}
async function cmdSkillReads(argv) {
  const json = argv.includes('--json');
  const agent = argv.filter((a) => a !== '--json')[0];
  if (!agent) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon skill reads <agent> [--json]\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const j = await http('GET', `/api/agents/${encodeURIComponent(agent)}/skill-reads`);
  if (json) {
    process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j, null, 2) + '\n');
    return;
  }
  const rows = Object.entries(j.skills || {}).sort((a, b) => b[1].reads - a[1].reads);
  process.stdout.write(`${j.agent ?? agent}: ${j.missions ?? 0} mission(s) in ${j.window_days ?? 30} days\n`);
  if (!rows.length) {
    process.stdout.write('no skill read\n');
    return;
  }
  for (const [id, s] of rows) process.stdout.write(`  ${id}  ${s.reads} read(s), ${s.missions} mission(s)\n`);
}

async function cmdSkill(argv) {
  const [sub, ...rest] = argv;
  switch (sub) {
    case 'attach':
      return cmdSkillAttach(rest);
    case 'detach':
      return cmdSkillDetach(rest);
    case 'attachments':
      return cmdSkillAttachments(rest);
    case 'resolve':
      return cmdSkillResolve(rest);
    case 'reads':
      return cmdSkillReads(rest);
    case 'list':
      return cmdSkillList();
    case 'get':
      return cmdSkillGet(rest);
    case 'put':
      return cmdSkillPut(rest);
    case 'rm':
    case 'delete':
      return cmdSkillRm(rest);
    default:
      process.stderr.write('usage: timon skill <list|get|put|rm|attach|detach|attachments|resolve|reads> …\n');
      process.exit(64);
  }
}

/* ─── mcp ─── */
async function cmdMcpList() {
  const j = await http('GET', '/api/mcp');
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j.servers || [], null, 2) + '\n');
}
async function cmdMcpGet(argv) {
  const id = argv[0];
  if (!id) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon mcp get <id>\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const j = await http('GET', `/api/mcp/${encodeURIComponent(id)}`);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j, null, 2) + '\n');
}
async function cmdMcpPut(argv) {
  const id = argv.shift();
  if (!id) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon mcp put <id> [--file PATH]  (or pipe JSON on stdin)\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const raw = await readContent(argv, 'MCP JSON config');
  let parsed;
  try {
    parsed = JSON.parse(raw);
  } catch (e) {
    process.stderr.write('timon: invalid JSON — ' + e.message + '\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  if (!parsed.transport) {
    process.stderr.write('timon: payload must include "transport" (stdio or http)\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const body = { id, ...parsed };
  const j = await http('POST', '/api/mcp', body);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j, null, 2) + '\n');
}
async function cmdMcpRm(argv) {
  const id = argv[0];
  if (!id) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon mcp rm <id>\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const j = await http('DELETE', `/api/mcp/${encodeURIComponent(id)}`);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j) + '\n');
}

async function cmdMcp(argv) {
  const [sub, ...rest] = argv;
  switch (sub) {
    case 'list':
      return cmdMcpList();
    case 'get':
      return cmdMcpGet(rest);
    case 'put':
      return cmdMcpPut(rest);
    case 'rm':
    case 'delete':
      return cmdMcpRm(rest);
    default:
      process.stderr.write('usage: timon mcp <list|get|put|rm> …\n');
      process.exit(64);
  }
}

/* ─── agents (create / update) ──────────────────────────────────────────
   Deletion stays manual (rm -rf ~/.timon/agents/<name>) — too easy to
   nuke a config by reflex, no CLI shortcut for it. */

const AGENT_CONFIG_KEYS = [
  'backend', 'model', 'permission_mode', 'cwd', 'project',
  'allowed_tools', 'disallowed_tools',
  'skills', 'mcp_servers', 'excluded_mcp_servers',
  'memory_scope', 'look', 'avatar',
];

/** Pull config flags off argv and return them as a partial AgentConfig.
 *  String fields: --backend, --model, --permission-mode, --cwd, --project.
 *  Array fields: --skills, --mcp-servers, --allowed-tools, --disallowed-tools,
 *                --excluded-mcp-servers (each accepts a comma-separated list,
 *                or repeat the flag to append).
 *  JSON field: --look (mascot look object, or null).
 *  --avatar emoji|image|mascot (null clears it). */
function takeConfigFlags(argv) {
  const cfg = {};
  const strFlags = [
    ['backend', 'backend'],
    ['model', 'model'],
    ['permission-mode', 'permission_mode'],
    ['cwd', 'cwd'],
    ['project', 'project'],
  ];
  for (const [flag, key] of strFlags) {
    const v = takeFlag(argv, flag);
    if (v !== undefined) cfg[key] = v;
  }
  const arrFlags = [
    ['skills', 'skills'],
    ['mcp-servers', 'mcp_servers'],
    ['allowed-tools', 'allowed_tools'],
    ['disallowed-tools', 'disallowed_tools'],
    ['excluded-mcp-servers', 'excluded_mcp_servers'],
  ];
  for (const [flag, key] of arrFlags) {
    const items = [];
    // repeat flag → accumulate; comma-separated values → split
    while (true) {
      const v = takeFlag(argv, flag);
      if (v === undefined) break;
      items.push(...v.split(',').map((s) => s.trim()).filter(Boolean));
    }
    if (items.length) cfg[key] = items;
  }
  // The daemon checks the values and names the wrong one; only the JSON is read here.
  const look = takeFlag(argv, 'look');
  if (look !== undefined) {
    try {
      cfg.look = JSON.parse(look);
    } catch {
      process.stderr.write(`timon: --look expects JSON, e.g. '{"shape":"round","color":"#d4a373","eyes":"happy","acc":"none"}' (or null to clear it)\n`);
      process.exit(64);
    }
  }
  // Checked by the daemon too; `null` is the only word read here.
  const avatar = takeFlag(argv, 'avatar');
  if (avatar !== undefined) cfg.avatar = avatar === 'null' ? null : avatar;
  return cfg;
}

async function cmdAgentCreate(argv) {
  const name = argv.shift();
  if (!name) {
    process.stderr.write(
      'usage: timon agent create <name> [--prompt-file PATH] [--backend …] [--model …] …\n' +
      '       (system prompt: pipe on stdin or pass --prompt-file)\n',
    );
    process.exit(64);
  }
  // Refuse to clobber an existing agent — `agent update` is the right tool.
  const probe = await httpRaw('GET', `/api/agents/${encodeURIComponent(name)}`);
  if (probe.ok) {
    process.stderr.write(`timon: agent "${name}" already exists — use \`timon agent update\`\n`);
    process.exit(1);
  }
  const config = takeConfigFlags(argv);
  // The usage line says --prompt-file; readContent only knows --file.
  const promptFile = takeFlag(argv, 'prompt-file');
  if (promptFile) argv.push('--file', promptFile);
  const system_prompt = (await readContent(argv, 'system prompt')).replace(/\s+$/, '') + '\n';
  if (!system_prompt.trim()) {
    process.stderr.write('timon: empty system prompt\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const j = await http('POST', '/api/agents', {
    name, system_prompt,
    config: Object.keys(config).length ? config : undefined,
  });
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j, null, 2) + '\n');
}

async function cmdAgentUpdate(argv) {
  const name = argv.shift();
  if (!name) {
    process.stderr.write(
      'usage: timon agent update <name> [--prompt-file PATH] [--backend …] [--model …] …\n' +
      '       (everything optional; supply only the fields to change)\n',
    );
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const current = await httpRaw('GET', `/api/agents/${encodeURIComponent(name)}`);
  if (!current.ok) {
    process.stderr.write(`timon: agent "${name}" not found — use \`timon agent create\`\n`);
    process.exit(1);
  }
  const cfgPatch = takeConfigFlags(argv);
  const promptFile = takeFlag(argv, 'prompt-file');
  // Read new prompt only if explicitly requested (file or stdin-with-content);
  // without --prompt-file and with a TTY stdin we leave the prompt untouched.
  let newPrompt = null;
  if (promptFile) {
    newPrompt = fs.readFileSync(promptFile, 'utf8');
  } else if (!process.stdin.isTTY) {
    const piped = await readAll(process.stdin);
    if (piped.trim()) newPrompt = piped;
  }

  if (newPrompt != null) {
    // Prompt changes require POST /api/agents (full upsert). Merge the
    // existing config with the patch so we don't drop unrelated fields.
    const mergedCfg = {};
    // Same round-trip as the MCP `agent_update` (mcp-tools-agents.mjs): the
    // editable config keys plus the fields the full upsert would otherwise
    // erase (role, picture, context, browser profile).
    for (const k of [...AGENT_CONFIG_KEYS, ...PRESERVED_ON_REWRITE]) {
      if (current.body[k] !== undefined && current.body[k] !== null) {
        // listAgents returns [] defaults — treat empty arrays as "absent"
        // so we don't bloat config.json with noise on round-trip.
        if (Array.isArray(current.body[k]) && current.body[k].length === 0) continue;
        mergedCfg[k] = current.body[k];
      }
    }
    Object.assign(mergedCfg, cfgPatch);
    const j = await http('POST', '/api/agents', {
      name, system_prompt: newPrompt,
      config: Object.keys(mergedCfg).length ? mergedCfg : undefined,
    });
    process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j, null, 2) + '\n');
    return;
  }

  if (Object.keys(cfgPatch).length === 0) {
    process.stderr.write('timon: nothing to update — pass --prompt-file/stdin or any --config flag\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const j = await http('PATCH', `/api/agents/${encodeURIComponent(name)}/config`, cfgPatch);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j, null, 2) + '\n');
}

async function cmdAgentSetScope(argv) {
  const VALID_SCOPES = ['NONE', 'SESSION', 'AGENT', 'GLOBAL'];
  const [name, scope] = argv;
  if (!name || !scope) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon agent set-scope <name> <NONE|SESSION|AGENT|GLOBAL>\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  if (!VALID_SCOPES.includes(scope.toUpperCase())) {
    process.stderr.write(`timon: invalid scope "${scope}" — must be one of ${VALID_SCOPES.join(', ')}\n`);
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const j = await http('PATCH', `/api/agents/${encodeURIComponent(name)}/config`, {
    memory_scope: scope.toUpperCase(),
  });
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j, null, 2) + '\n');
}

async function cmdAgentSetAvatar(argv) {
  const clear = argv.includes('--clear');
  const rest = argv.filter((a) => a !== '--clear');
  const [name, file] = rest;
  if (!name || rest.length > 2 || (clear ? file !== undefined : !file)) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon agent set-avatar <name> <image-file> | timon agent set-avatar <name> --clear\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  let body;
  try {
    body = clear ? { clear: true } : readAvatarFile(file);
  } catch (err) {
    process.stderr.write(`timon: ${err.message}\n`);
    process.exit(1);
  }
  const j = await http('PUT', `/api/agents/${encodeURIComponent(name)}/avatar`, body);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j, null, 2) + '\n');
}

async function cmdAgentRename(argv) {
  const [from, to] = argv;
  if (!from || !to || argv.length > 2) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon agent rename <old-name> <new-name>\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const j = await http('POST', `/api/agents/${encodeURIComponent(from)}/rename`, { newName: to });
  for (const w of j.warnings ?? []) process.stderr.write(`timon: warning: ${w}\n`);
  for (const t of j.triggers_to_check ?? []) process.stderr.write(`timon: warning: trigger "${t.name}": ${t.reason}\n`);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j, null, 2) + '\n');
}

const AGENT_TRASH_USAGE = 'usage: timon agent trash <list [--json] | restore <id> | purge <id>>\n';

/** Deleted agents (TODO #476): list them, put one back, or empty one entry for good. */
async function cmdAgentTrash(argv) {
  const [sub, ...rest] = argv;
  const entryPath = (id) => `/api/agent-trash/${encodeURIComponent(id)}`;
  switch (sub) {
    case 'list':
    case undefined: {
      const j = await http('GET', '/api/agent-trash');
      if (rest.includes('--json')) { process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j, null, 2) + '\n'); return; }
      const entries = Array.isArray(j.entries) ? j.entries : [];
      const purge = !j.enabled ? 'trash off: deletions are final'
        : j.retention_days > 0 ? `purged ${j.retention_days} days after deletion` : 'kept until purged by hand';
      process.stdout.write(`agent trash (${entries.length}) — ${purge}\n`);
      for (const e of entries) {
        const by = e.deleted_by ? ` by ${e.deleted_by}` : '';
        const until = e.expires_at ? `, purge ${formatTs(e.expires_at)}` : '';
        process.stdout.write(`  ${e.id}  ${e.name}  deleted ${formatTs(e.deleted_at)}${by}${until}\n`);
      }
      return;
    }
    case 'restore': {
      const [id] = rest;
      if (!id || rest.length > 1) { process.stderr.write(AGENT_TRASH_USAGE); process.exit(64); }
      const j = await http('POST', `${entryPath(id)}/restore`, {});
      process.stdout.write(`restored ${j.name}\n`);
      return;
    }
    case 'purge': {
      const [id] = rest;
      if (!id || rest.length > 1) { process.stderr.write(AGENT_TRASH_USAGE); process.exit(64); }
      await http('DELETE', entryPath(id));
      process.stdout.write(`purged ${id}\n`);
      return;
    }
    default:
      process.stderr.write(AGENT_TRASH_USAGE);
      process.exit(64);
  }
}

const AGENT_DOC_USAGE = 'usage: timon agent doc <list <agent> | get <agent> <file> | put <agent> <file> [--file PATH] | rm <agent> <file>>\n';

/** Identity docs of an agent (SOUL.md…): the routes of the app's identity editor. */
async function cmdAgentDoc(argv) {
  const [sub, ...rest] = argv;
  const docPath = (agent, file) => `/api/agents/${encodeURIComponent(agent)}/docs${file === undefined ? '' : `/${encodeURIComponent(file)}`}`;
  switch (sub) {
    case 'list': {
      const [agent] = rest;
      if (!agent || rest.length > 1) { process.stderr.write(AGENT_DOC_USAGE); process.exit(64); }
      const j = await http('GET', docPath(agent));
      process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j.files || [], null, 2) + '\n');
      return;
    }
    case 'get': {
      const [agent, file] = rest;
      if (!agent || !file || rest.length > 2) { process.stderr.write(AGENT_DOC_USAGE); process.exit(64); }
      const j = await http('GET', `${docPath(agent, file)}?format=json`);
      // A daemon older than the CLI ignores ?format=json and sends the text itself.
      process.stdout.write(typeof j?.content === 'string' ? j.content : typeof j === 'string' ? j : JSON.stringify(j));
      return;
    }
    case 'put': {
      const agent = rest.shift();
      const file = rest.shift();
      if (!agent || !file) { process.stderr.write(AGENT_DOC_USAGE); process.exit(64); }
      const content = await readContent(rest, 'doc content');
      if (rest.length > 0) { process.stderr.write(AGENT_DOC_USAGE); process.exit(64); }
      // An empty write would wipe the doc: deleting is `rm`, said explicitly.
      if (!content.trim()) { process.stderr.write('timon: empty content (to delete the doc: timon agent doc rm)\n'); process.exit(64); }
      const j = await http('PUT', docPath(agent, file), { content });
      // A daemon older than the CLI reads a JSON body as an empty doc and says 200.
      if (typeof j?.size === 'number' && j.size !== Buffer.byteLength(content, 'utf8')) {
        process.stderr.write(`timon: the daemon stored ${j.size} bytes instead of ${Buffer.byteLength(content, 'utf8')}: it is older than this CLI, restart Timon after the update\n`);
        process.exit(2);
      }
      process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j) + '\n');
      return;
    }
    case 'rm':
    case 'delete': {
      const [agent, file] = rest;
      if (!agent || !file || rest.length > 2) { process.stderr.write(AGENT_DOC_USAGE); process.exit(64); }
      const j = await http('DELETE', docPath(agent, file));
      process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j) + '\n');
      return;
    }
    default:
      process.stderr.write(AGENT_DOC_USAGE);
      process.exit(64);
  }
}

/** What `timon agent export|import` needs from this CLI: the daemon, files, a question. */
function agentTransferIo() {
  return {
    api: () => API,
    headers: timonHeaders,
    takeFlag,
    cwd: () => process.cwd(),
    readFile: (path) => fs.readFileSync(path),
    writeFile: (path, bytes, opts) => fs.writeFileSync(path, bytes, opts),
    isTTY: () => process.stdin.isTTY === true,
    ask: async (question) => {
      const readline = await import('node:readline/promises');
      const rl = readline.createInterface({ input: process.stdin, output: process.stdout });
      try { return await rl.question(question); } finally { rl.close(); }
    },
    out: (text) => process.stdout.write(text),
    err: (text) => process.stderr.write(text),
    exit: (code) => process.exit(code),
  };
}

async function cmdAgent(argv) {
  const [sub, ...rest] = argv;
  switch (sub) {
    case 'create':
      return cmdAgentCreate(rest);
    case 'update':
      return cmdAgentUpdate(rest);
    case 'set-scope':
      return cmdAgentSetScope(rest);
    case 'set-avatar':
      return cmdAgentSetAvatar(rest);
    case 'rename':
      return cmdAgentRename(rest);
    case 'doc':
    case 'docs':
      return cmdAgentDoc(rest);
    case 'trash':
      return cmdAgentTrash(rest);
    case 'export':
      return cmdAgentExport(rest, agentTransferIo());
    case 'import':
      return cmdAgentImport(rest, agentTransferIo());
    case 'export-skill':
      return cmdAgentExportSkill(rest, agentTransferIo());
    default:
      process.stderr.write(
        'usage: timon agent <create|update|set-scope|set-avatar|rename|doc|trash|export|import|export-skill> <name> …\n' +
        '       (deletion: the app or the agent_delete tool, which move the agent to the trash)\n',
      );
      process.exit(64);
  }
}

/* ─── mission (summarize / fork) ───────────────────────────────────────
   Cross-provider continuation. Summarize compresses the transcript via
   the mission's current backend; fork spawns a new mission on a target
   agent seeded with that summary — so e.g. a Claude conversation can
   keep going on Codex when Claude rate-limits. */

async function cmdMissionSummarize(argv) {
  const id = argv.shift();
  if (!id) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon mission summarize <mission_id> [--force]\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const force = argv.includes('--force');
  const j = await http('POST', `/api/missions/${encodeURIComponent(id)}/summarize`, { force });
  process.stderr.write(`[${j.cached ? 'cached' : 'fresh'} summary, through event #${j.eventId}]\n`);
  process.stdout.write(j.summary + '\n');
}

async function cmdMissionFork(argv) {
  const id = argv.shift();
  if (!id) {
    process.stderr.write(
      'usage: timon mission fork <mission_id> --to <agent> [--message "..."]\n',
    );
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const target = takeFlag(argv, 'to');
  const message = takeFlag(argv, 'message');
  if (!target) {
    process.stderr.write('timon: --to <agent> required\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const j = await http('POST', `/api/missions/${encodeURIComponent(id)}/fork`, {
    agent: target,
    message,
  });
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({ mission_id: j.missionId, cached_summary: j.cached }) + '\n');
}

/** `timon mission search <text…>` — find a past conversation.
 *
 *  Exists because until 2026-08-23, the only way to search mission
 *  history was to open timon.db in sqlite3 and type a LIKE by hand.
 *  Searches the initial prompt of missions and the text of assistant/user
 *  turns — not tool outputs (1GB of tool_result that's never what you're
 *  looking for when you're looking for a conversation). */
async function cmdMissionSearch(argv) {
  const agent = takeFlag(argv, 'agent');
  const project = takeFlag(argv, 'project');
  const since = takeFlag(argv, 'since');
  const until = takeFlag(argv, 'until');
  const limit = takeFlag(argv, 'limit');
  const json = argv.includes('--json');
  const q = joinRest(argv.filter((a) => a !== '--json'), 0).trim();
  if (!q) {
    process.stderr.write(
      'usage: timon mission search <text…> [--agent NAME] [--project SLUG]\n' +
      '                            [--since 7d|ISO] [--until 7d|ISO] [--limit N] [--json]\n',
    );
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const params = new URLSearchParams({ q });
  if (agent) params.set('agent', agent);
  if (project) params.set('project', project);
  if (since) params.set('since', since);
  if (until) params.set('until', until);
  if (limit) params.set('limit', limit);
  const j = await http('GET', `/api/missions/search?${params.toString()}`);
  if (json) {
    process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j, null, 2) + '\n');
    return;
  }
  for (const h of j.hits || []) {
    const when = new Date(h.ts).toISOString().replace('T', ' ').slice(0, 16);
    const label = h.task_title ? ` · ${h.task_title}` : '';
    process.stdout.write(`${h.mission_id}  ${when}  [${h.agent_name}/${h.role}]${label}\n`);
    process.stdout.write(`  ${String(h.snippet || '').replace(/\s+/g, ' ')}\n`);
  }
  const p = j.progress || {};
  const partial = p.done === false
    ? `  ⚠ index still catching up (${p.cursor}/${p.maxEventId} events) — retry later`
    : '';
  process.stdout.write(`\n${j.count || 0} excerpt(s) for "${q}"${partial}\n`);
}

/** `timon mission reindex` — manual catch-up of the search index.
 *  The orchestrator already does this on its own as a background task at
 *  boot; this command is for forcing it, or watching progress. */
async function cmdMissionReindex(argv) {
  const batch = Number(takeFlag(argv, 'batch') || 500);
  let total = 0;
  for (;;) {
    const r = await http('POST', '/api/missions/search/reindex', { batch });
    total += r.indexed || 0;
    process.stderr.write(`\r  ${r.cursor}/${r.maxEventId} events · ${total} fragments indexed`);
    if (r.done) break;
  }
  process.stderr.write('\n');
  process.stdout.write(`index up to date — ${total} fragment(s) added\n`);
}

/** `timon mission permission-mode get|set` — the permission level of a
 *  running mission, on the route the composer's selector uses (TODO #569).
 *  The daemon holds the whole guard (owner scope, spawn grid, caller
 *  ceiling, audit of refusals): the CLI only relays, so a refusal comes back
 *  as the route's 403 with its reason, never as a local guess. */
async function cmdMissionPermissionMode(argv) {
  const [sub, id, mode] = argv;
  const usage =
    'usage: timon mission permission-mode get <mission_id>\n' +
    '       timon mission permission-mode set <mission_id> <mode>\n';
  if (sub === 'get' && id) {
    const j = await http('GET', `/api/missions/${encodeURIComponent(id)}/permission-mode`);
    process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j) + '\n');
    return;
  }
  if (sub === 'set' && id && mode) {
    const j = await http('POST', `/api/missions/${encodeURIComponent(id)}/permission-mode`, { mode });
    process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j) + '\n');
    return;
  }
  process.stderr.write(usage);
  process.exit(64);
}

/** `timon mission egress <id>` — the mission's journaled outbound connections
 *  (TODO #590). The route holds the access rule (owner scope, 404 for someone
 *  else's mission); the CLI only relays and prints the JSON. */
async function cmdMissionEgress(argv) {
  const limit = takeFlag(argv, 'limit');
  const before = takeFlag(argv, 'before');
  const id = argv[0];
  if (!id) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon mission egress <mission_id> [--limit N] [--before ID]\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const query = new URLSearchParams();
  if (limit !== undefined) query.set('limit', limit);
  if (before !== undefined) query.set('before', before);
  const qs = query.toString();
  const j = await http('GET', `/api/missions/${encodeURIComponent(id)}/egress${qs ? `?${qs}` : ''}`);
  // On stderr too: piped into `jq .connections`, stdout alone would read as "no connection".
  if (j.notice) process.stderr.write(`${j.notice}\n`);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j, null, 2) + '\n');
}

async function cmdMission(argv) {
  const [sub, ...rest] = argv;
  switch (sub) {
    case 'summarize':
      return cmdMissionSummarize(rest);
    case 'fork':
      return cmdMissionFork(rest);
    case 'search':
      return cmdMissionSearch(rest);
    case 'reindex':
      return cmdMissionReindex(rest);
    case 'permission-mode':
      return cmdMissionPermissionMode(rest);
    case 'egress':
      return cmdMissionEgress(rest);
    default:
      process.stderr.write('usage: timon mission <summarize|fork|search|reindex|permission-mode|egress> …\n');
      process.exit(64);
  }
}

/* ─── tasks ─── */
async function cmdTaskList(argv) {
  const status = takeFlag(argv, 'status');
  // full=1: the list trims long texts by default (the board's view); the
  // CLI keeps printing every task exactly as stored.
  const path = status ? `/api/tasks?full=1&status=${encodeURIComponent(status)}` : '/api/tasks?full=1';
  const j = await http('GET', path);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j.tasks || [], null, 2) + '\n');
}

async function cmdTaskGet(argv) {
  const id = argv[0];
  if (!id) { process.stderr.write('usage: timon task get <id>\n'); process.exit(64); }
  const j = await http('GET', `/api/tasks/${id}`);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j.task, null, 2) + '\n');
}

async function cmdTaskCreate(argv) {
  const title = takeFlag(argv, 'title') || joinRest(argv, 0);
  const agent = takeFlag(argv, 'agent');
  const description = takeFlag(argv, 'description');
  const priority = takeFlag(argv, 'priority');
  const deps = takeFlag(argv, 'deps');
  const scheduled = takeFlag(argv, 'scheduled');
  const extraSkills = takeFlag(argv, 'extra-skills');
  const extraMcp = takeFlag(argv, 'extra-mcp');
  const allow = takeFlag(argv, 'allow');
  const type = takeFlag(argv, 'type');
  const backend = takeFlag(argv, 'backend');
  const model = takeFlag(argv, 'model');
  // EXPLICIT fallback for THIS task (takes priority over the series and the
  // global setting): --fallback-backend none = no auto fallback for it.
  const fallbackBackend = takeFlag(argv, 'fallback-backend');
  const fallbackModel = takeFlag(argv, 'fallback-model');
  const permission = takeFlag(argv, 'permission-mode');
  // --group-id: documented by the timon-task skill for a long time but never
  // read here — tasks created via the CLI had no group, and the wake-loop's
  // "group done" wakeup never fired for them.
  const groupId = takeFlag(argv, 'group-id');
  // --plan-group: the group of volets of the series plan (`kanban_plan`) the
  // task belongs to. Its review, merge, doc and iterations inherit it, and all
  // of them resolve on `timon series role|fallback set --group NAME` first.
  const planGroup = takeFlag(argv, 'plan-group');
  const pipeline = takeFlag(argv, 'pipeline');
  // --project: forces the task's project slug instead of letting it derive
  // from the assigned agent. An agent outside any project gave a null slug →
  // no review/merge role resolved and auto-chaining stayed silent.
  const project = takeFlag(argv, 'project');
  // Starting branch of the worktree: without it, the worktree inherits the current
  // branch of the shared repo, whichever another agent happens to be on.
  const base = takeFlag(argv, 'base');
  // TO DO idea this task implements: it closes itself once the chain lands.
  const todo = takeFlag(argv, 'todo');

  if (!title || !agent) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon task create --title TEXT --agent NAME [--description D] [--priority 1-5]\n' +
      '       [--type code|review|merge|research|doc|chore] [--project SLUG] [--base BRANCH]\n' +
      '       [--pipeline full|code-self|code-group] [--group-id ID] [--plan-group NAME] [--todo ID]\n' +
      '       [--backend NAME] [--model SLUG] [--permission-mode default|acceptEdits|bypassPermissions]\n' +
      '       [--fallback-backend NAME|none] [--fallback-model SLUG]\n' +
      '       [--deps id1,id2] [--scheduled ISO] [--extra-skills s1,s2] [--extra-mcp m1,m2]\n' +
      '       [--allow "Bash(timon:*),Read(/tmp/*)"]\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  await assertBackend('task create', backend);
  if (pipeline && !['full', 'code-self', 'code-group'].includes(pipeline)) {
    process.stderr.write(`timon task create: --pipeline must be 'full', 'code-self' or 'code-group' (got: ${pipeline})\n`);
    process.exit(64);
  }
  if (todo !== undefined && todo !== null && !/^[1-9]\d*$/.test(todo)) {
    process.stderr.write(`timon task create: --todo must be a TO DO item id (got: ${todo})\n`);
    process.exit(64);
  }

  const body = {
    title,
    agent_name: agent,
    description: description || undefined,
    priority: priority ? Number(priority) : undefined,
    type: type || undefined,
    deps: deps ? deps.split(',').map(s => s.trim()).filter(Boolean) : undefined,
    scheduled_at: scheduled ? new Date(scheduled).getTime() : undefined,
    extra_skills: extraSkills ? extraSkills.split(',').map(s => s.trim()).filter(Boolean) : undefined,
    extra_mcp_servers: extraMcp ? extraMcp.split(',').map(s => s.trim()).filter(Boolean) : undefined,
    extra_allowed_tools: allow ? allow.split(',').map(s => s.trim()).filter(Boolean) : undefined,
    backend_override: backend || undefined,
    model_override: model || undefined,
    fallback_backend_override: fallbackBackend || undefined,
    fallback_model_override: fallbackModel || undefined,
    permission_mode_override: permission || undefined,
    group_id: groupId || undefined,
    plan_group: planGroup || undefined,
    pipeline: pipeline || undefined,
    project: project || undefined,
    base: base || undefined,
    todo_id: todo ? Number(todo) : undefined,
    trace_id: process.env.TIMON_TRACE_ID || undefined,
  };

  const j = await http('POST', '/api/tasks', body);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j.task, null, 2) + '\n');
}

async function cmdTaskDone(argv) {
  const id = argv[0];
  if (!id) { process.stderr.write('usage: timon task done <id> [--comment TEXT | --comment-file PATH | --comment-stdin] [--merged-sha SHA] [--summary TEXT]\n'); process.exit(64); }
  // Comment: --comment TEXT (inline, short) OR --comment-file PATH OR
  // --comment-stdin (reads stdin). The last two avoid any shell-quoting
  // truncation when the agent produces a long done_comment (e.g. a verbose
  // review JSON). The verification-loop parses the verdict; a truncated
  // inline comment broke the JSON and stalled the chain in BLOCKED.
  let comment = takeFlag(argv, 'comment');
  const commentFile = takeFlag(argv, 'comment-file');
  const wantStdin = argv.includes('--comment-stdin')
    ? (argv.splice(argv.indexOf('--comment-stdin'), 1), true)
    : false;
  if (comment === undefined && commentFile) {
    comment = fs.readFileSync(commentFile, 'utf8');
  } else if (comment === undefined && wantStdin) {
    if (process.stdin.isTTY) { process.stderr.write('timon: --comment-stdin requires piped input\n'); process.exit(64); }
    comment = await readAll(process.stdin);
  }
  const mergedSha = takeFlag(argv, 'merged-sha');
  const summary = takeFlag(argv, 'summary');
  // If the merger agent performed a merge → record the sha BEFORE marking
  // DONE. The orchestrator's merge guard refuses a type='merge' task's DONE
  // transition without merged_commit_sha: the reverse order would make the
  // legitimate transition fail (degraded to BLOCKED). The branch can be
  // cleaned up afterward via `timon worktree dispose`, the audit trail
  // remains via the sha + DB events.
  if (mergedSha) {
    await http('POST', `/api/tasks/${id}/merged-sha`, { sha: mergedSha });
  }
  const update = { status: 'DONE', done_comment: comment };
  if (summary) update.done_summary = summary;
  await http('PUT', `/api/tasks/${id}`, update);
  process.stdout.write(`task ${id} → DONE\n`);
  if (comment) process.stdout.write(`comment: ${comment}\n`);
  if (mergedSha) process.stdout.write(`merged sha: ${mergedSha}\n`);
}

/**
 * TIM-0109 — a branch merged outside Timon (a PR merged on GitHub, a merge by
 * hand): records its merge commit on a blocked task, or on a done one that
 * has none, so the tasks that depend on it can start. The daemon checks the
 * commit against the task's base branch.
 */
async function cmdTaskMarkMerged(argv) {
  const id = argv[0] && !argv[0].startsWith('--') ? argv.shift() : undefined;
  const sha = takeFlag(argv, 'sha');
  const comment = takeFlag(argv, 'comment');
  if (!id || !sha) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon task mark-merged <id> --sha SHA [--comment TEXT]\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const j = await http('POST', `/api/tasks/${encodeURIComponent(id)}/mark-merged`, { sha, ...(comment ? { comment } : {}) });
  process.stdout.write(`task ${id} marked merged: ${sha}${j?.verified === false ? ' (commit not found locally: not verified)' : ''}\n`);
}

/** Reads the closing comment: inline, from a file, or from redirected stdin.
 *  The last two avoid any shell-quoting truncation on a long comment. */
async function readClosingComment(argv) {
  let comment = takeFlag(argv, 'comment');
  const commentFile = takeFlag(argv, 'comment-file');
  const wantStdin = argv.includes('--comment-stdin')
    ? (argv.splice(argv.indexOf('--comment-stdin'), 1), true)
    : false;
  if (comment === undefined && commentFile) return fs.readFileSync(commentFile, 'utf8');
  if (comment === undefined && wantStdin) {
    if (process.stdin.isTTY) { process.stderr.write('timon: --comment-stdin requires piped input\n'); process.exit(64); }
    return await readAll(process.stdin);
  }
  return comment;
}

/**
 * Typed closing gesture: the task is resolved from the CURRENT MISSION
 * server-side (X-TIMON-Mission, sent on every call by `timonHeaders`), so there
 * is no id to copy from the brief — that was the first cause of a task never
 * being closed. The comment is mandatory: the daemon refuses a mute closure.
 * `timon task done` stays valid, it is just the variant that requires an id.
 */
async function cmdTaskMarkAsDone(argv) {
  const id = argv[0] && !argv[0].startsWith('--') ? argv.shift() : undefined;
  const comment = await readClosingComment(argv);
  const verdict = takeFlag(argv, 'verdict');
  const mergedSha = takeFlag(argv, 'merged-sha');
  const summary = takeFlag(argv, 'summary');
  if (!comment) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon task mark-as-done [id] --comment TEXT | --comment-file PATH | --comment-stdin\n' +
      '       [--verdict pass|changes_requested] [--merged-sha SHA] [--summary TEXT]\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const body = { outcome: 'done', comment };
  if (id) body.id = id;
  if (verdict) body.verdict = verdict;
  if (mergedSha) body.merged_sha = mergedSha;
  if (summary) body.summary = summary;
  const j = await http('POST', '/api/tasks/close', body);
  process.stdout.write(`task ${j.task.id} → DONE\n`);
  if (j.task.merged_commit_sha) process.stdout.write(`merged sha: ${j.task.merged_commit_sha}\n`);
}

async function cmdTaskMarkAsFailed(argv) {
  const id = argv[0] && !argv[0].startsWith('--') ? argv.shift() : undefined;
  const reason = takeFlag(argv, 'reason');
  if (!reason) { process.stderr.write('usage: timon task mark-as-failed [id] --reason TEXT\n'); process.exit(64); }
  const body = { outcome: 'failed', reason };
  if (id) body.id = id;
  const j = await http('POST', '/api/tasks/close', body);
  process.stdout.write(`task ${j.task.id} → BLOCKED (${reason})\n`);
}

async function cmdTaskBlock(argv) {
  const id = argv[0];
  if (!id) { process.stderr.write('usage: timon task block <id> --reason ...\n'); process.exit(64); }
  const reason = takeFlag(argv, 'reason');
  if (!reason) { process.stderr.write('timon task block: --reason is required\n'); process.exit(64); }
  await http('PUT', `/api/tasks/${id}`, { status: 'BLOCKED', blocked_reason: reason });
  process.stdout.write(`task ${id} → BLOCKED (${reason})\n`);
}

async function cmdTaskUpdate(argv) {
  const id = argv[0];
  if (!id) { process.stderr.write('usage: timon task update <id> [--status ...] [--priority N] [--title ...] [--scheduled ISO | --clear-scheduled]\n'); process.exit(64); }
  const fields = {};
  const status = takeFlag(argv, 'status');
  const priority = takeFlag(argv, 'priority');
  const title = takeFlag(argv, 'title');
  const agent = takeFlag(argv, 'agent');
  const description = takeFlag(argv, 'description');
  const scheduled = takeFlag(argv, 'scheduled');
  // Unscheduling requires an explicit flag: `scheduled_at: null` stays a
  // no-op on the API side (null = "field not provided"), otherwise a client
  // resubmitting its whole form would wipe the scheduling by accident.
  const clearScheduled = argv.includes('--clear-scheduled');
  const blocked_reason = takeFlag(argv, 'blocked-reason');
  const done_comment = takeFlag(argv, 'done-comment');
  const extraSkills = takeFlag(argv, 'extra-skills');
  const extraMcp = takeFlag(argv, 'extra-mcp');
  const allow = takeFlag(argv, 'allow');
  const type = takeFlag(argv, 'type');
  const backend = takeFlag(argv, 'backend');
  const model = takeFlag(argv, 'model');
  const fallbackBackend = takeFlag(argv, 'fallback-backend');
  const fallbackModel = takeFlag(argv, 'fallback-model');
  const permission = takeFlag(argv, 'permission-mode');
  await assertBackend('task update', backend);
  if (status) fields.status = status;
  if (priority) fields.priority = Number(priority);
  if (title) fields.title = title;
  if (agent) fields.agent_name = agent;
  if (description) fields.description = description;
  if (scheduled) fields.scheduled_at = new Date(scheduled).getTime();
  if (clearScheduled) fields.clear_scheduled_at = true;
  if (blocked_reason) fields.blocked_reason = blocked_reason;
  if (done_comment) fields.done_comment = done_comment;
  if (extraSkills) fields.extra_skills = extraSkills.split(',').map(s => s.trim()).filter(Boolean);
  if (extraMcp) fields.extra_mcp_servers = extraMcp.split(',').map(s => s.trim()).filter(Boolean);
  if (allow) fields.extra_allowed_tools = allow.split(',').map(s => s.trim()).filter(Boolean);
  if (backend) fields.backend_override = backend;
  if (model) fields.model_override = model;
  if (fallbackBackend) fields.fallback_backend_override = fallbackBackend;
  if (fallbackModel) fields.fallback_model_override = fallbackModel;
  if (permission) fields.permission_mode_override = permission;
  if (type) fields.type = type;
  const j = await http('PUT', `/api/tasks/${id}`, fields);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j.task, null, 2) + '\n');
}

async function cmdTaskDelete(argv) {
  const chain = argv.includes('--chain');
  const id = argv.find((a) => a !== '--chain');
  if (!id) { process.stderr.write('usage: timon task delete <id> [--chain]\n'); process.exit(64); }
  const j = await http('DELETE', `/api/tasks/${encodeURIComponent(id)}${chain ? '?chain=1' : ''}`);
  const count = Array.isArray(j?.deleted) ? j.deleted.length : 1;
  process.stdout.write(count > 1 ? `task ${id} and ${count - 1} chain task(s) deleted\n` : `task ${id} deleted\n`);
}

async function cmdTask(argv) {
  const [sub, ...rest] = argv;
  switch (sub) {
    case 'list':    return cmdTaskList(rest);
    case 'get':     return cmdTaskGet(rest);
    case 'create':  return cmdTaskCreate(rest);
    case 'done':    return cmdTaskDone(rest);
    case 'block':   return cmdTaskBlock(rest);
    case 'mark-as-done':   return cmdTaskMarkAsDone(rest);
    case 'mark-as-failed': return cmdTaskMarkAsFailed(rest);
    case 'mark-merged':    return cmdTaskMarkMerged(rest);
    case 'update':  return cmdTaskUpdate(rest);
    case 'delete':  return cmdTaskDelete(rest);
    case 'rm':      return cmdTaskDelete(rest);
    default:
      process.stderr.write('usage: timon task <list|get|create|done|block|mark-as-done|mark-as-failed|mark-merged|update|delete> …\n');
      process.exit(64);
  }
}

/* ─── backend catalog ─── */

/** What's REALLY available here and now: a profile whose credentials were
 *  missing when the orchestrator started doesn't appear. This is the only
 *  legitimate source for proposing a fallback backend — a list from memory
 *  would propose unconfigured providers. */
async function cmdBackends(argv) {
  const json = argv.includes('--json');
  const r = await http('GET', '/api/backends/catalog');
  if (json) { process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(r, null, 2) + '\n'); return; }
  for (const b of r.backends ?? []) {
    const models = (b.models ?? []).map((m) => m.slug);
    process.stdout.write(`${b.id.padEnd(14)} ${b.label ?? ''}\n`);
    if (b.defaultModel) process.stdout.write(`  default: ${b.defaultModel}\n`);
    if (models.length) process.stdout.write(`  models: ${models.join(', ')}\n`);
  }
}

/* ─── series fallback plan ─── */

/**
 * `timon series fallback` — which backend takes over, and for WHOM, when
 * quota runs out mid-chantier.
 *
 * Three scopes suffice in practice:
 *   orchestrator  the mission driving the series. It receives all the
 *                 alerts: if it goes down, the chantier stops even when the
 *                 rest of the fleet still has quota.
 *   code          the coder, the chantier's main model. Its fallback must be
 *                 of the same caliber — a long task picked up by a small
 *                 model produces code that will need redoing.
 *   *             everything else (review, merge, doc, chore): a small
 *                 model is usually enough.
 * A precise type (`--scope review`) takes priority over `*` if set.
 *
 * Without `--series`, the targeted series is the one driven by the current
 * mission (`TIMON_MISSION_ID`) — even when it doesn't have a task yet: the
 * series' future identity is already known, it's this mission.
 */
async function cmdSeriesFallback(argv) {
  const [sub, ...rest] = argv;
  const series = takeFlag(rest, 'series') || 'current';
  if (sub === 'list' || sub === undefined) {
    const out = await http('GET', `/api/series/${encodeURIComponent(series)}/fallbacks`);
    if (!out.fallbacks?.length) {
      process.stdout.write(`series ${out.series_id}: no fallback plan (global setting applies)\n`);
      return;
    }
    process.stdout.write(`series ${out.series_id}\n`);
    for (const f of out.fallbacks) {
      const target = f.backend ? `${f.backend}${f.model ? ` / ${f.model}` : ''}` : 'no fallback (failure accepted)';
      // A group rule is read before the series one for the tasks of that group.
      const where = f.plan_group ? ` [group ${f.plan_group}]` : '';
      process.stdout.write(`  ${f.scope.padEnd(13)} → ${target}${where}\n`);
    }
    return;
  }
  if (sub === 'set') {
    const scope = takeFlag(rest, 'scope');
    const backend = takeFlag(rest, 'backend');
    const model = takeFlag(rest, 'model');
    const group = takeFlag(rest, 'group');
    if (!scope) {
      process.stderr.write(
        'usage: timon series fallback set --scope orchestrator|code|review|merge|doc|chore|* \n' +
        '         --backend NAME [--model SLUG] [--group NAME] [--series ID] [--no-apply]\n' +
        '       --backend none  → this scope does not fall back (failure accepted)\n' +
        '       --group NAME    → rule of ONE group of volets of the plan (never with orchestrator)\n' +
        '       --no-apply      → record the rule only, do not move the pending tasks\n');
      process.exit(64);
    }
    if (backend && backend !== 'none') await assertBackend('series fallback set', backend);
    // A rule posted mid-chantier is APPLIED right away: the PENDING/BLOCKED tasks
    // the scope governs move onto it now. Posting it before the tasks exist
    // changes nothing (nothing to move); `--no-apply` records it and touches
    // nothing, deliberately.
    const apply = !rest.includes('--no-apply');
    const body = {
      scope, backend: backend === 'none' ? null : backend, model: model ?? null, apply,
      ...(group ? { group } : {}),
    };
    const out = await http('PUT', `/api/series/${encodeURIComponent(series)}/fallbacks`, body);
    process.stdout.write(`series ${out.series_id}: ${scope}${group ? ` [group ${group}]` : ''} → ${body.backend ?? 'no fallback'}${body.model ? ` / ${body.model}` : ''}\n`);
    if (out.apply_error) {
      process.stdout.write(`  rule recorded, but applying it failed: ${out.apply_error}\n`);
    } else if (!apply) {
      process.stdout.write('  recorded only (--no-apply): running tasks were not moved\n');
    } else if (out.applied) {
      process.stdout.write(
        `  applied now: pending tasks of this scope moved to ${out.applied.backend}` +
        `${out.applied.model ? ` / ${out.applied.model}` : ''}\n`);
    } else {
      process.stdout.write('  nothing to move right now (no pending task on this scope)\n');
    }
    return;
  }
  if (sub === 'clear') {
    const scope = takeFlag(rest, 'scope');
    const group = takeFlag(rest, 'group');
    if (!scope) { process.stderr.write('usage: timon series fallback clear --scope SCOPE [--group NAME] [--series ID]\n'); process.exit(64); }
    const query = group ? `?group=${encodeURIComponent(group)}` : '';
    const out = await http('DELETE', `/api/series/${encodeURIComponent(series)}/fallbacks/${encodeURIComponent(scope)}${query}`);
    process.stdout.write(`series ${out.series_id}: rule ${scope}${group ? ` [group ${group}]` : ''} removed\n`);
    return;
  }
  process.stderr.write('usage: timon series fallback <list|set|clear> …\n');
  process.exit(64);
}

/**
 * `timon series role` — backend/model of a task type for ONE series.
 *
 * The series planner's per-role picks land here rather than in `roles.json`:
 * the project default must not change because one chantier wanted another
 * reviewer. Read at dispatch, so the review/merge/doc tasks the orchestrator
 * creates later inherit it through their series alone.
 */
async function cmdSeriesRole(argv) {
  const [sub, ...rest] = argv;
  const series = takeFlag(rest, 'series') || 'current';
  if (sub === 'list' || sub === undefined) {
    const out = await http('GET', `/api/series/${encodeURIComponent(series)}/roles`);
    if (!out.roles?.length) {
      process.stdout.write(`series ${out.series_id}: no role choice (project roles apply)\n`);
      return;
    }
    process.stdout.write(`series ${out.series_id}\n`);
    for (const r of out.roles) {
      // A group choice governs the tasks created with `--plan-group` and their chain.
      const where = r.plan_group ? ` [group ${r.plan_group}]` : '';
      process.stdout.write(`  ${r.scope.padEnd(9)} → ${r.backend ?? '(project backend)'}${r.model ? ` / ${r.model}` : ''}${where}\n`);
    }
    return;
  }
  if (sub === 'set') {
    const scope = takeFlag(rest, 'scope');
    const backend = takeFlag(rest, 'backend');
    const model = takeFlag(rest, 'model');
    const group = takeFlag(rest, 'group');
    if (!scope || (!backend && !model)) {
      process.stderr.write(
        'usage: timon series role set --scope code|review|merge|research|doc|chore\n' +
        '         [--backend NAME] [--model SLUG] [--group NAME] [--series ID]   (at least one of backend/model)\n' +
        '       --group NAME → choice of ONE group of volets of the plan (tasks created with --plan-group)\n');
      process.exit(64);
    }
    if (backend) await assertBackend('series role set', backend);
    const out = await http('PUT', `/api/series/${encodeURIComponent(series)}/roles`, {
      scope, backend: backend ?? null, model: model ?? null, ...(group ? { group } : {}),
    });
    process.stdout.write(`series ${out.series_id}: ${scope}${group ? ` [group ${group}]` : ''} → ${backend ?? '(project backend)'}${model ? ` / ${model}` : ''}\n`);
    return;
  }
  if (sub === 'clear') {
    const scope = takeFlag(rest, 'scope');
    const group = takeFlag(rest, 'group');
    if (!scope) { process.stderr.write('usage: timon series role clear --scope SCOPE [--group NAME] [--series ID]\n'); process.exit(64); }
    const query = group ? `?group=${encodeURIComponent(group)}` : '';
    const out = await http('DELETE', `/api/series/${encodeURIComponent(series)}/roles/${encodeURIComponent(scope)}${query}`);
    process.stdout.write(`series ${out.series_id}: role ${scope}${group ? ` [group ${group}]` : ''} removed${group ? '' : ' (project roles apply)'}\n`);
    return;
  }
  process.stderr.write('usage: timon series role <list|set|clear> …\n');
  process.exit(64);
}

async function cmdSeries(argv) {
  const [sub, ...rest] = argv;
  switch (sub) {
    case 'fallback': return cmdSeriesFallback(rest);
    case 'role': return cmdSeriesRole(rest);
    default:
      process.stderr.write('usage: timon series <fallback|role> <list|set|clear> …\n');
      process.exit(64);
  }
}

/* ─── worktrees ─── */
async function cmdWorktreeInfo(argv) {
  const id = argv[0];
  if (!id) { process.stderr.write('usage: timon worktree info <task-id>\n'); process.exit(64); }
  const j = await http('GET', `/api/tasks/${id}`);
  const t = j.task;
  if (!t) { process.stderr.write('task not found\n'); process.exit(2); }
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({
    task_id: t.id,
    worktree_path: t.worktree_path,
    branch_name: t.branch_name,
    base_branch: t.base_branch,
    merged_commit_sha: t.merged_commit_sha,
  }, null, 2) + '\n');
}

async function cmdWorktreeCreate(argv) {
  const id = argv[0];
  if (!id) { process.stderr.write('usage: timon worktree create <task-id> [--base BRANCH]\n'); process.exit(64); }
  const base = takeFlag(argv, 'base');
  const j = await http('POST', `/api/tasks/${id}/worktree`, base ? { base } : {});
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j.worktree, null, 2) + '\n');
}

async function cmdWorktreeDispose(argv) {
  const id = argv[0];
  if (!id) { process.stderr.write('usage: timon worktree dispose <task-id> [--force]\n'); process.exit(64); }
  const force = argv.includes('--force');
  const j = await http('DELETE', `/api/tasks/${id}/worktree${force ? '?force=1' : ''}`);
  process.stdout.write(`worktree for task ${id}: ${j.disposed ? 'disposed' : 'no-op (none attached)'}\n`);
}

async function cmdWorktree(argv) {
  const [sub, ...rest] = argv;
  switch (sub) {
    case 'info':    return cmdWorktreeInfo(rest);
    case 'create':  return cmdWorktreeCreate(rest);
    case 'dispose': return cmdWorktreeDispose(rest);
    case 'rm':      return cmdWorktreeDispose(rest);
    default:
      process.stderr.write('usage: timon worktree <info|create|dispose> <task-id> …\n');
      process.exit(64);
  }
}

/* ─── projects (agent roles per project) ─── */
async function cmdProjectList() {
  const j = await http('GET', '/api/projects');
  // GET /api/projects returns {slug, name, …} objects; a bare slug is still accepted.
  for (const p of j.projects) process.stdout.write((typeof p === 'string' ? p : p.slug) + '\n');
}

async function cmdProjectRoles(argv) {
  const slug = argv[0];
  if (!slug) { process.stderr.write('usage: timon project roles <slug>\n'); process.exit(64); }
  const j = await http('GET', `/api/projects/${encodeURIComponent(slug)}/roles`);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j.roles, null, 2) + '\n');
}

async function cmdProjectSetRole(argv) {
  // takeFlag mutates argv → extract the flags first so that the remaining
  // positionals are slug / role / agent.
  const backend = takeFlag(argv, 'backend');
  const model = takeFlag(argv, 'model');
  const permission = takeFlag(argv, 'permission-mode');
  const [slug, role, agent] = argv;
  if (!slug || !role || agent === undefined) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon project set-role <slug> <code|review|merge|research|doc|chore> <agent-name>\n' +
      '       [--backend NAME] [--model SLUG] [--permission-mode default|acceptEdits|bypassPermissions]\n' +
      '       timon project set-role <slug> <role> ""   (to clear)\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  await assertBackend('project set-role', backend);
  const body = agent === '' ? {} : { agent };
  if (backend) body.backend = backend;
  if (model) body.model = model;
  if (permission) body.permission_mode = permission;
  const j = await http('PATCH', `/api/projects/${encodeURIComponent(slug)}/roles/${encodeURIComponent(role)}`, body);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j.roles, null, 2) + '\n');
}

const PROJECT_META_FLAGS = ['name', 'cwd', 'workspace', 'color', 'icon', 'speech', 'kind', 'status'];

/** `project create|update`: same body as the MCP tools. An unknown workspace is refused unless --create-workspace. */
async function cmdProjectWrite(verb, argv) {
  const createWorkspace = argv.includes('--create-workspace');
  const rest = argv.filter((a) => a !== '--create-workspace');
  const body = { workspace_policy: createWorkspace ? 'create' : 'existing' };
  for (const key of PROJECT_META_FLAGS) {
    const value = takeFlag(rest, key);
    if (value !== undefined) body[key] = value;
  }
  const slug = rest[0];
  if (!slug || rest.length > 1) {
    process.stderr.write(`usage: timon project ${verb} <slug> [--name TEXT] [--cwd PATH] [--workspace NAME] [--create-workspace]\n` +
      '       [--color #RRGGBB] [--icon TEXT] [--speech TEXT] [--kind TEXT] [--status TEXT]\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  if (verb === 'create') {
    const j = await http('POST', '/api/projects', { ...body, slug });
    process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j.warnings?.length ? { ...j.project, warnings: j.warnings } : j.project, null, 2) + '\n');
    return;
  }
  const j = await http('PUT', `/api/projects/${encodeURIComponent(slug)}/meta`, body);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({ slug, ...j.meta, ...(j.warnings?.length ? { warnings: j.warnings } : {}) }, null, 2) + '\n');
}

async function cmdWorkspace(argv) {
  const [sub, ...rest] = argv;
  if (sub !== 'list') {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon workspace list [--json]\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const j = await http('GET', '/api/workspaces');
  if (rest.includes('--json')) {
    process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j.workspaces ?? [], null, 2) + '\n');
    return;
  }
  for (const w of j.workspaces ?? []) {
    process.stdout.write(`${w.name} (${w.slug})  lead: ${w.lead_agent ?? '-'}  projects: ${w.projects.length ? w.projects.join(', ') : '-'}\n`);
  }
}

async function cmdProject(argv) {
  const [sub, ...rest] = argv;
  switch (sub) {
    case 'list':      return cmdProjectList();
    case 'roles':     return cmdProjectRoles(rest);
    case 'set-role':  return cmdProjectSetRole(rest);
    case 'create':
    case 'update':    return cmdProjectWrite(sub, rest);
    case 'demo': {
      const j = await http('POST', '/api/projects/demo', {});
      process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j) + '\n');
      return;
    }
    default:
      process.stderr.write('usage: timon project <list|roles|set-role|create|update|demo> …\n');
      process.exit(64);
  }
}

/* ─── agent messages (inter-agent async) ─── */

async function cmdMsgSend(argv) {
  const inReplyTo = takeFlag(argv, 'in-reply-to');
  const kind = takeFlag(argv, 'kind');
  const toMission = takeFlag(argv, 'to-mission');
  const to = argv[0];
  const payload = joinRest(argv, 1).trim();
  if (!to || !payload) {
    process.stderr.write(
      'usage: timon msg send <to_agent> <payload...>\n' +
      '       [--kind msg|request|response] [--in-reply-to <msg_id>] [--to-mission <mid>]\n',
    );
    process.exit(64);
  }
  if (!process.env.TIMON_MISSION_ID) {
    process.stderr.write('timon msg send: TIMON_MISSION_ID required (must run inside an agent)\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const body = { to_agent: to, payload };
  if (process.env.TIMON_TRACE_ID) body.trace_id = process.env.TIMON_TRACE_ID;
  if (kind) body.kind = kind;
  if (inReplyTo) body.in_reply_to = inReplyTo;
  if (toMission) body.to_mission = toMission;
  const j = await http('POST', '/api/messages', body);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j) + '\n');
}

async function cmdMsgRecv(argv) {
  const fromAgent = takeFlag(argv, 'from');
  const status = takeFlag(argv, 'status') || 'pending';
  const limit = takeFlag(argv, 'limit');
  const to = takeFlag(argv, 'to') || process.env.TIMON_AGENT;
  if (!to) {
    process.stderr.write('timon msg recv: --to <agent> required (or set TIMON_AGENT)\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const qs = new URLSearchParams({ to, status });
  if (fromAgent) qs.set('from', fromAgent);
  if (limit) qs.set('limit', limit);
  const j = await http('GET', `/api/messages?${qs.toString()}`);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j.messages || [], null, 2) + '\n');
}

async function cmdMsgPick(argv) {
  const id = argv[0];
  if (!id) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon msg pick <message_id>\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const j = await http('POST', `/api/messages/${encodeURIComponent(id)}/pick`);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j.message, null, 2) + '\n');
}

async function cmdMsgReply(argv) {
  const id = argv.shift();
  const payload = joinRest(argv, 0).trim();
  if (!id || !payload) {
    process.stderr.write('usage: timon msg reply <message_id> <payload...>\n');
    process.exit(64);
  }
  const ref = await http('GET', `/api/messages/${encodeURIComponent(id)}`);
  const orig = ref.message;
  if (!orig) {
    process.stderr.write(`timon msg reply: message ${id} not found\n`);
    process.exit(2);
  }
  const body = {
    to_agent: orig.from_agent,
    to_mission: orig.from_mission,
    kind: 'response',
    in_reply_to: id,
    payload,
  };
  const j = await http('POST', '/api/messages', body);
  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(j) + '\n');
}

async function cmdMsg(argv) {
  const [sub, ...rest] = argv;
  switch (sub) {
    case 'send':  return cmdMsgSend(rest);
    case 'recv':  return cmdMsgRecv(rest);
    case 'pick':  return cmdMsgPick(rest);
    case 'reply': return cmdMsgReply(rest);
    default:
      process.stderr.write('usage: timon msg <send|recv|pick|reply> …\n');
      process.exit(64);
  }
}

